From: Mamuthka linux
Subject: [PATCH] dpu20: decon_probe error path must not hang in kthread_stop()

When the DT lacks the panel lcd_info (e.g. recovery.img without
recovery_dtbo: S-Boot then applies no overlay), dsim reports 0x0 resolution,
decon_acquire_windows() fails on a zero-size ION allocation and decon_probe()
unwinds through decon_destroy_vsync_thread().  kthread_stop() only wakes the
vsync thread, but its wait_event_interruptible() condition does not include
kthread_should_stop(), so the thread goes straight back to sleep and PID 1
(kernel_init) stays in D state forever.  Measured on SM-A515F: init stuck,
then 4 s later "tzdev: iwsock error. result=11" panic -> bootloop.

- vsync thread: wake up on kthread_should_stop() and leave the loop before
  touching DECON registers (the pmOS framebuffer hack restarts DECON there).
- decon_probe(): do not kfree() the devm_kzalloc()'d decon (double free at
  devres release) and clear decon_drvdata[] so nobody sees a freed struct.

The system then continues to boot without a display instead of hanging.

---
diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
index e77c9e7..57a0d32 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
@@ -4219,9 +4219,16 @@ err_psr:
 err_vsync:
 	iounmap(decon->res.ss_regs);
 err_res:
-	kfree(decon);
+	/*
+	 * Mamuthka: a decon devm_kzalloc()-kal foglalt, a kfree() itt dupla
+	 * felszabadítás lenne (a devres a probe hibája után maga szabadítja
+	 * fel). A globális mutatót is töröljük, hogy más driverek ne egy
+	 * felszabadított struktúrát lássanak.
+	 */
+	if (decon_drvdata[decon->id] == decon)
+		decon_drvdata[decon->id] = NULL;
 err:
-	decon_err("decon probe fail");
+	decon_err("decon probe fail (ret=%d): no display, boot continues\n", ret);
 	return ret;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_dsi.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_dsi.c
index 1189735..61d8672 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_dsi.c
@@ -332,14 +332,25 @@ static int decon_vsync_thread(void *data)
 		ktime_t timestamp = decon->vsync.timestamp;
 #if defined(CONFIG_SUPPORT_KERNEL_4_9)
 		int ret = wait_event_interruptible(decon->vsync.wait,
-			!ktime_equal(timestamp, decon->vsync.timestamp) &&
-			decon->vsync.active);
+			(!ktime_equal(timestamp, decon->vsync.timestamp) &&
+			decon->vsync.active) || kthread_should_stop());
+		if (kthread_should_stop())
+			break;
 #else
 		int ret = wait_event_interruptible(decon->vsync.wait,
-			(timestamp != decon->vsync.timestamp) &&
-			decon->vsync.active);
+			((timestamp != decon->vsync.timestamp) &&
+			decon->vsync.active) || kthread_should_stop());
 			
 		struct decon_mode_info psr;		
+		/*
+		 * Mamuthka: kthread_stop() csak felébreszti a szálat; a feltétel
+		 * nélküle hamis maradna, és a szál örökre visszaaludna, a
+		 * decon_destroy_vsync_thread() (decon_probe hibaága) pedig a
+		 * kthread_stop()-ban ragadna (PID 1 D állapotban). Leállításkor
+		 * a DECON-regiszterekhez sem nyúlunk (a hibaág utána unmap-el).
+		 */
+		if (kthread_should_stop())
+			break;
 		if (needs_pan) {
 			// TODO: This is dirty hack.
 			// Implement a better solution
